WEBVTT

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
♪Medallion

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
♪Machinegun Shower

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
♪Florsheim's

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
♪Florsheim monster

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪Florsheim monster

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪Curse of the Ancients

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪Deadly Infiltration Plan

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪Geirus

00:00.003 --> 00:01.436
♪Simple Tarako Spaghetti Menu

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪Khamenman

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪The next day...

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪Florsheim monster

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪Emphatic!

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪Yesterday♪

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪Do not enter!

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪Mosqui

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪Very Sexy Paradise

00:01.460 --> 00:03.389
I know it was you!

00:03.390 --> 00:04.779
I don't know what you're talking about!

00:04.780 --> 00:06.299
Hey, are you trying to one-up me?

00:06.300 --> 00:06.850
What?

00:06.851 --> 00:08.850
What are you talking about?

00:09.200 --> 00:11.799
You knew it was mine, didn't you?

00:11.800 --> 00:13.620
I told you I didn't know!

00:14.290 --> 00:15.950
Don't you remember yesterday...

00:17.340 --> 00:18.669
Did you go to the convenience store?

00:18.670 --> 00:19.670
Yeah.

00:19.940 --> 00:22.179
Check it out. I bet you
don't see <i>these</i> everyday.

00:22.180 --> 00:25.360
They just started selling those
right? That's some high quality stuff.

00:25.410 --> 00:29.639
Yeah, I always keep an eye out
for new cup noodles floating around.

00:29.640 --> 00:30.949
You sure love those noodles.

00:30.950 --> 00:33.299
Well, the market for cup noodles
is quite competitive after all.

00:33.300 --> 00:36.689
Products disappear in the
blink of an eye don't they?

00:36.690 --> 00:38.000
Yeah, they sure do!

00:39.140 --> 00:40.799
You were there, weren't you?

00:40.800 --> 00:43.279
Why the hell would I be eavesdropping?

00:43.280 --> 00:45.869
Huh? What's going on here?

00:45.870 --> 00:46.470
Oh, Master Vamp.

00:46.471 --> 00:48.219
Hear me out here.

00:48.220 --> 00:51.599
Damn Khamenman ate the
cup noodles I was saving for later.

00:51.600 --> 00:53.730
I said I didn't do it!

00:54.480 --> 00:55.640
He did what to your noodles?!

02:26.450 --> 02:28.120
He did what to your noodles?!

02:33.360 --> 02:35.559
I guess I got all surprised for nothing.

02:35.560 --> 02:37.879
I don't know if I should call
you Ramen or Khamen, but...

02:37.880 --> 02:40.609
Asshole! You just have to
keep milking that one, don't you?

02:40.610 --> 02:43.349
Just because it was funny once
doesn't mean it doesn't get old!

02:43.350 --> 02:44.270
What the hell?

02:44.271 --> 02:47.609
Did you think that I might not notice,
and you'd somehow get away with this?

02:47.610 --> 02:48.190
Quit bitching!

02:48.191 --> 02:51.059
And stop shaking my chin
else it's going to pop off!

02:51.060 --> 02:52.449
I'll melt yo' punk ass!

02:52.450 --> 02:54.360
I'll curse you to hell!

02:54.900 --> 02:57.199
All right, stop it you two.

02:57.200 --> 02:59.530
You didn't know it was his
ramen right, Khamenman?

03:01.120 --> 03:01.650
Y-Yeah...

03:01.651 --> 03:03.169
Bullshit.

03:03.170 --> 03:05.069
Come on, stop fighting.

03:05.070 --> 03:07.449
I'll pay for the noodles if
that's what you're worried about.

03:07.450 --> 03:09.269
Go buy yourself a new one, Medallion.

03:09.270 --> 03:10.910
Why not three or four while you're at it?

03:11.440 --> 03:12.440
Eh?

03:13.450 --> 03:14.450
What is this...

03:15.490 --> 03:16.730
What do you think you're doing?

03:18.630 --> 03:21.060
He's the one who should be paying!

03:21.480 --> 03:22.890
Huh? What? What's happening?

03:24.690 --> 03:27.359
You shouldn't have done that Mr. Vamp.

03:27.360 --> 03:27.980
Really?

03:27.980 --> 03:28.810
Yeah.

03:28.811 --> 03:32.129
If you just give him money like that,
Medallion can't prove his point anymore.

03:32.130 --> 03:35.289
He'll probably realize how pathetic he was
for fighting over a bowl of cup noodles.

03:35.290 --> 03:38.899
The part where you said "why not three or
four" was probably the icing on the cake.

03:38.900 --> 03:40.849
Oh and also the part where you said
"if that's what you're worried about."

03:40.850 --> 03:44.479
It kind of sounds like you're indirectly
trying to one-up him by saying,

03:44.480 --> 03:45.919
"I got bank, bitch."

03:45.920 --> 03:48.150
Exactly. I was thinking the same thing.

03:49.860 --> 03:52.730
W-Why do I have to take all the blame?

03:53.240 --> 03:57.119
They were supposed to
fight Red together this time,

03:57.120 --> 04:00.110
so I was only trying to get
them to be friends again!

04:03.340 --> 04:04.860
Fine, see if I care!

04:06.680 --> 04:07.680
Ah...

04:10.780 --> 04:12.580
Medallion's not coming, is he.

04:13.520 --> 04:17.199
Well, I'm not going to just
sit around. I'm heading out.

04:17.200 --> 04:19.599
Huh? I thought we were meeting at two?

04:19.600 --> 04:22.140
Medallion's not picking up.

04:25.460 --> 04:26.990
See if I care about that punk.

04:34.060 --> 04:40.630
But I bet it'd be really awkward if
he went and got beat up by himself.

04:41.530 --> 04:43.330
Go to hell, Sunred!

04:47.880 --> 04:51.179
Jesus, are you guys even trying anymore?

04:51.180 --> 04:52.980
I thought you guys
were an evil organization.

04:53.020 --> 04:54.170
Damn it...

04:59.000 --> 05:00.000
Ah.

05:00.480 --> 05:01.480
Sorry I'm late.

05:02.320 --> 05:03.430
Take this!

05:03.860 --> 05:06.470
Twin Death Attack!

05:17.550 --> 05:18.490
Here's a tissue.

05:18.490 --> 05:19.490
T-Thanks.

05:21.590 --> 05:24.299
Sorry I ate your noodles without asking.

05:24.300 --> 05:26.940
Nah, sorry for being all anal and shit.

05:27.540 --> 05:30.669
I just couldn't admit it at the time.

05:30.670 --> 05:32.789
It happens, man.

05:32.790 --> 05:34.639
Aren't you glad that they're friends again?

05:34.640 --> 05:35.460
Yup.

05:35.461 --> 05:37.742
Now there's just one more
person we need to take care of.

05:37.830 --> 05:40.129
Master Vamp, dinner's ready!

05:40.130 --> 05:42.600
We made your favorite oden soup today!

05:43.770 --> 05:44.770
I'm not hungry.

05:53.170 --> 05:55.100
Hey, I brought some backup.

05:55.510 --> 05:56.510
Huh?

05:56.650 --> 05:57.680
Come in already!

05:59.610 --> 06:00.940
Excuse us.

06:04.470 --> 06:06.309
Ah, you must be Vamp!

06:06.310 --> 06:08.329
Nice to meet you, My name is Uchida Kayoko.

06:08.330 --> 06:10.499
Nice to meet you too.

06:10.500 --> 06:11.930
I've heard so much about you.

06:12.640 --> 06:15.819
I'm sorry to make you
guys help out with the move.

06:15.820 --> 06:17.330
Huh? Move?

06:17.960 --> 06:22.510
Oh, it looks like he called
us to help him move in.

06:23.610 --> 06:25.959
My heart just skipped a beat!

06:25.960 --> 06:28.279
Mr. Red didn't tell us anything after all.

06:28.280 --> 06:33.569
I thought he was going to drag us somewhere
shady and beat the living shit out of us.

06:33.570 --> 06:35.349
Yeah, totally dude.

06:35.350 --> 06:38.179
Huh? He didn't just call you
guys out of the blue, did he?

06:38.180 --> 06:40.449
I'm sorry if we interrupted anything...

06:40.450 --> 06:41.450
Oh no, not at all!

06:41.930 --> 06:45.980
We wouldn't be where we are right
now if it wasn't for Mr. Red, you know.

06:48.250 --> 06:49.289
Isn't that right, Mr. Red?

06:49.290 --> 06:50.280
Shut your trap!

06:50.281 --> 06:53.809
Oh, now I understand why you
asked for monsters that can fly.

06:53.810 --> 06:57.459
You wanted us to help you carry
stuff over through the sky, right?

06:57.460 --> 06:58.320
Yeah.

06:58.321 --> 07:02.119
There's still the fridge and some other stuff
over at the old place, so go get those for me.

07:02.120 --> 07:02.880
Yes, sir.

07:02.881 --> 07:04.959
Oh, Mosqui, I'm sorry
to bother you with this,

07:04.960 --> 07:07.979
but can you go grab my
apron from our secret base?

07:07.980 --> 07:09.959
Wow, you're asking me?

07:09.960 --> 07:10.530
Delighted to, sir.

07:10.531 --> 07:12.489
You guys better not drop anything!

07:12.490 --> 07:13.490
Understood!

07:14.220 --> 07:17.829
Oh and also bring me the detergent I
always use around the house, Mosqui.

07:17.830 --> 07:18.830
Okay!

07:29.160 --> 07:30.880
Huh? What's this?

07:31.810 --> 07:32.810
Holy shit!

07:33.210 --> 07:34.479
Keep it down!

07:34.480 --> 07:36.139
I'm trying to keep this
a secret from Kayoko.

07:36.140 --> 07:39.019
Holy crap man, I so wanted to see this!

07:39.020 --> 07:41.809
I'll let you have it so
don't tell the others, okay?

07:41.810 --> 07:43.979
For real? Holy shit...

07:43.980 --> 07:45.539
I said shut up about it!

07:45.540 --> 07:46.549
Huh, what's going on?

07:46.550 --> 07:47.550
Stay away from this room!

07:48.200 --> 07:51.779
Oh, you use <i>this brand Vamp?</i>

07:51.780 --> 07:54.209
Isn't this the American kind
that they only sell by mail order?

07:54.210 --> 07:55.389
Oh yeah.

07:55.390 --> 07:56.499
Does it work well?

07:56.500 --> 07:59.369
It's pretty much the same
as the other detergents,

07:59.370 --> 08:06.069
but I like it because it's made of natural
eco-friendly ingredients like coconut oil.

08:06.070 --> 08:06.870
Wow.

08:06.871 --> 08:09.999
Kayoko, should I just put the
chopsticks in the kitchen drawer?

08:10.000 --> 08:11.739
Yeah, just stick them in there.

08:11.740 --> 08:15.199
Oh yeah, did you see that
"hide and something" movie?

08:15.200 --> 08:19.299
Oh, I watched it when I went
out to Shinjuku that other time.

08:19.300 --> 08:20.929
Kayoko, where's the cutter?

08:20.930 --> 08:22.349
It should be around there.

08:22.350 --> 08:23.880
Did you even look for it?

08:24.510 --> 08:27.689
The kid in that movie
was really cute, right?

08:27.690 --> 08:31.680
Yeah, the movie definitely
got a boost because of that kid.

08:32.600 --> 08:35.299
Those things emit heat from the back so make
sure to place it away from the wall a little.

08:35.300 --> 08:36.090
Yes, sir.

08:36.091 --> 08:38.679
And be sure not to scratch
the frame with your beak, okay?

08:38.680 --> 08:39.680
Yes, sir.

08:42.160 --> 08:42.510
Here you go.

08:42.511 --> 08:45.109
Damn, this incandescent
light's a piece of work.

08:45.110 --> 08:47.899
You guys are so helpful.

08:47.900 --> 08:50.150
Unlike somebody I know...

08:50.990 --> 08:51.990
What?

08:52.070 --> 08:56.139
Oh, fluorine-coated pots get scratched easily
if you stack them up like that Mr. Red.

08:56.140 --> 08:57.759
God, shut up!

08:57.760 --> 09:00.319
Weren't you guys supposed to be
conquering the world or something?

09:00.320 --> 09:03.839
Come on, he's helping out here,
you didn't have to hit him like that!

09:03.840 --> 09:05.089
This is none of your business.

09:05.090 --> 09:06.289
What did you say?

09:06.290 --> 09:10.019
I-It's ok Kayoko, I'm used to it...

09:10.020 --> 09:12.189
I think you've said enough!

09:12.190 --> 09:14.099
I told you to stop!

09:14.100 --> 09:17.369
Who cares? These guys are part
of an evil organization, you know.

09:17.370 --> 09:20.609
Well right now, I can't tell
who's good and who's bad!

09:20.610 --> 09:21.480
Um...

09:21.481 --> 09:24.449
You're supposed to be the
good guy, so know your role!

09:24.450 --> 09:27.010
Oh god, here we go again.

09:31.360 --> 09:34.609
Don't you think the air's
kind of tense in here?

09:34.610 --> 09:38.030
It'll all be over soon, so let's just
concentrate on cleaning up for now.

09:38.350 --> 09:39.350
Okay.

09:40.310 --> 09:42.860
Wow, I never thought it'd
be done in just half a day.

09:43.970 --> 09:46.599
It's all thanks to you guys, Vamp.

09:46.600 --> 09:47.700
Oh no, not at all.

09:48.640 --> 09:51.269
Well, we better get going.

09:51.270 --> 09:52.519
Oh, hold on.

09:52.520 --> 09:54.639
Why don't you stay for
some celebratory soba?

09:54.640 --> 09:56.059
Oh no, it's okay.

09:56.060 --> 09:58.899
Don't worry about it! I have to
thank you one way or another.

09:58.900 --> 10:02.539
Ah, well, we didn't bring
housewarming gifts either so...

10:02.540 --> 10:05.020
He says he doesn't want any,
so why don't you just let him be.

10:06.290 --> 10:09.289
The combat goons probably
have some dinner ready for us,

10:09.290 --> 10:12.019
and if we fill up on soba we
probably won't be able to eat, so...

10:12.020 --> 10:13.020
excuse us.

10:16.120 --> 10:19.899
I wonder if Mr. Red's been
in a better mood since then.

10:19.900 --> 10:22.179
Damn, I feel like shit right now.

10:22.180 --> 10:25.029
I wonder if he'll let us off easy today.

10:25.030 --> 10:26.520
Hey, sorry to keep you waiting guys!

10:27.890 --> 10:28.540
Mr. Red!

10:28.541 --> 10:31.120
Nice day out today, isn't it?

10:31.700 --> 10:33.209
Um, Mr. Red?

10:33.210 --> 10:33.760
Huh?

10:33.761 --> 10:36.659
Did you and Kayoko...

10:36.660 --> 10:38.279
Yeah, we're good now.

10:38.280 --> 10:40.069
Oh, I see.

10:40.070 --> 10:41.929
It seems like he's feeling better now.

10:41.930 --> 10:44.049
Feeling a little <i>too</i> better, if you ask me.

10:44.050 --> 10:47.279
I had my doubts about the new place since it's only
about five minutes from your guys' secret base,

10:47.280 --> 10:53.629
but then I realized it's convenient since I won't
have to travel far to meet up with you guys.

10:53.630 --> 10:54.679
That's right.

10:54.680 --> 10:55.879
It's great, isn't it?

10:55.880 --> 10:56.620
All right then.

10:56.621 --> 10:58.060
Let's get right to it.

10:58.610 --> 10:59.610
Sure!

11:00.860 --> 11:02.839
Isn't moving great?

11:02.840 --> 11:04.699
Thanks for the help guys.

11:04.700 --> 11:06.790
Are you all right, Mosqui?

11:07.110 --> 11:08.329
Y-Yeah...

11:08.330 --> 11:11.679
His heavy blow is unaffected
by wavering moods.

11:11.680 --> 11:13.069
Astro Fighter Sunred.

11:13.070 --> 11:15.869
This is a story about the
conflict of good between evil

11:15.870 --> 11:18.000
that takes place in the city of Kawasaki.

11:19.700 --> 11:22.849
General Vamp's Quick Recipes!

11:22.850 --> 11:24.789
Hi everyone, Vamp here.

11:24.790 --> 11:27.259
You're watching our
memorable first episode.

11:27.260 --> 11:30.419
I'm a little embarassed that the
title of the show has my name in it,

11:30.420 --> 11:31.900
but I can't let that phase me, can I?

11:32.660 --> 11:35.569
Today we'll be cooking a
simple tarako spaghetti dish.

11:35.570 --> 11:39.500
I recommend you try this one. You don't need
a lot to make it, plus it's pretty simple.

11:40.730 --> 11:42.899
Well then, let me show you the ingredients:

11:42.900 --> 11:45.389
First you need a medium
sized piece of tarako,

11:45.390 --> 11:49.929
a slice of butter, which you can cut as
you see in the picture or to your liking,

11:49.930 --> 11:51.229
then some salt,

11:51.230 --> 11:53.109
and then about 1.5 servings of spaghetti.

11:53.110 --> 11:58.189
By the way, one serving of spaghetti will just about
fit the diameter of the top of a plastic bottle.

11:58.190 --> 12:00.540
Now, let's get to the cooking part.

12:01.370 --> 12:04.039
Sprinkle some salt into boiling
water and dump the pasta inside,

12:04.040 --> 12:05.850
and boil until it reaches desired softness.

12:06.720 --> 12:13.300
Next, knead the tarako and mix
it with butter while the pasta boils.

12:18.150 --> 12:20.099
And now, the climax!

12:20.100 --> 12:25.109
Take the pasta out of the pot, mix it into
the bowl with the tarako while it's still hot,

12:25.110 --> 12:27.110
and when everything's
all nice and mixed together,

12:27.830 --> 12:29.449
you're done.

12:29.450 --> 12:33.239
If you're too lazy to
serve it on a different dish,

12:33.240 --> 12:36.399
you can just eat it out of the
bowl you mixed the tarako with.

12:36.400 --> 12:38.040
That's all part of being young after all.

12:38.570 --> 12:41.439
If you want to season it,
salt would be the way to go;

12:41.440 --> 12:44.499
if your spaghetti's too bland,
try adding some salt to it.

12:44.500 --> 12:47.479
You can also try adding some
nori or lemon juice if you'd like.

12:47.480 --> 12:50.279
And that's all the time we have for
General Vamp's Quick Recipes today.

12:50.280 --> 12:51.979
See you later!

12:51.980 --> 12:54.380
It's not too hard, so I bet
even you could cook it, Mr. Red!

12:54.450 --> 12:56.749
What the hell do you
mean "even I" could cook it?!
